!! Proposed Definitions And Examples

;__be'e__ (COI): Vocative. Used to make a request to speak.
** Keywords: Request to send.
 be'e nolni'u io
 re'i
 xu do dunda lo sicni
 ''Pardon me, ma'am.''
 ''Yes?''
 ''Can you spare a dime?''



;__co'o__ (COI): Vocative. Used to express an acknowledgement of parting. (cf. tolrinsa)
** Keywords: Bye-bye, goodbye, farewell, so long, adieu, Godspeed.
 co'o ro do
 ''Goodbye, everyone!''



;__coi__ (COI): Vocative. Used to express greeting. (f. rinsa)
** Keywords: Hi, hello, howdy, hail, salaam.
 coi pe mi pendo do mo
 ''Hello my friend, what are you up to?''



;__coico'o__ (COI*): Vocative. Used to express greetings in passing.
** Keywords:



;__fe'o__ (COI): Vocative. Used to indicate the end of a discussion.
** Keywords: Over and out.



;__fi'i__ (COI): Vocative. Used to greet cordially a visitor or recent arrival, express hospitality.
** Keywords: Welcome, make yourself at home.
  fi'i djan mi'a denpa tu'a do
  ''Welcome, John! We were waiting for you.''



;__fi'inai__ (COI*): Vocative. Used to express inhospitality.
** Keywords:
  le'o ko na rivbi fi'i nai palci je tolvri danlu
  ''Grr! Avoid not, unwelcome evil and cowardly beast!'' 



;__je'e__ (COI): roger -- vocative: roger (ack) - negative acknowledge; used to acknowledge offers and thanks --
** Keywords:



;__je'enai__ (COI*): negative acknowledge -- vocative: roger (ack) - negative acknowledge; I didn't hear you --
** Keywords:



;__ju'i__ (COI): attention -- vocative: attention - at ease - ignore me --
** Keywords:



;__ju'icu'i__ (COI*): at ease -- vocative: attention - at ease - ignore me --
** Keywords:



;__ju'inai__ (COI*): ignore me -- vocative: attention - at ease - ignore me --
** Keywords:



;__ke'o__ (COI): please repeat -- vocative: please repeat --
** Keywords:



;__ki'e__ (COI): thanks -- vocative: thanks - no thanks to you --
** Keywords:



;__ki'enai__ (COI*): no thanks to you -- vocative: thanks - no thanks to you --
** Keywords:



;__mi'e__ (COI): self-introduction -- self vocative: self-introduction - denial of identity; identifies speaker --
** Keywords:



;__mi'enai__ (COI*): no, I am not -- self vocative: self-introduction - denial of identity; denies identity of speaker --
** Keywords:



;__mu'o__ (COI): over -- vocative: over (response OK) - more to come --
** Keywords:



;__mu'onai__ (COI*): more to come -- vocative: over (response OK) - more to come --
** Keywords:



;__nu'e__ (COI): promise -- vocative: promise - promise release - un-promise --
** Keywords:



;__nu'ecu'i__ (COI*): release from promise -- vocative: promise - promise release - un-promise --
** Keywords:



;__nu'enai__ (COI*): non-promise -- vocative: promise - promise release - un-promise --
** Keywords:



;__pe'u__ (COI): please -- vocative: please --
** Keywords:



;__re'i__ (COI): ready to receive -- vocative: ready to receive - not ready to receive --
** Keywords:



;__re'inai__ (COI*): not ready to receive -- vocative: ready to receive - not ready to receive --
** Keywords:



;__ta'a__ (COI): interruption -- vocative: interruption --
** Keywords:



;__vi'o__ (COI): wilco -- vocative: wilco (ack and will comply) --
** Keywords:



;__doi__ (DOI): vocative marker -- generic vocative marker; identifies intended listener; elidable after COI --
** Keywords:



;__doido'u__ (DOI*): O You! -- generic vocative address to intended listener; --
** Keywords:



;__do'u__ (DOhU): end vocative -- elidable terminator: end vocative (often elidable) --
** Keywords:


